      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What is a permit to work system?</h3><p>It is a formal way to allow high-risk work under set controls. That means hot work, confined space entry, electrical isolation and work at height. A competent person authorises the permit before work starts and closes it when work ends. The permit is the proof.</p><h3>Is a permit to work a legal requirement in the UK?</h3><p>No single law names a permit in every case. But the Health and Safety at Work etc Act 1974, the Confined Spaces Regulations 1997 and the Work at Height Regulations 2005 require a safe system of work. A permit is the usual way to show it. This is not legal advice.</p><h3>Can I run a permit to work over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. You confirm each check by text, voice note or photo. No app and no login for the person on site. When you say done, Quickler writes the permit Record.</p><h3>Does the app replace the competent authoriser or the gas monitor?</h3><p>No. A competent person still authorises the work. An atmosphere test is read from a calibrated instrument. Quickler records the result. It does not assess risk, authorise entry or measure the air.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/compliance-audit-software-uk.html\">Compliance audit software for multi-site organisations</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/contractor-compliance-audit-uk.html\">Contractor compliance and induction audits</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/internal-audit-checklist-app-uk.html\">Internal audit checklist app (ISO 9001, 14001, 45001)</a></li></ul>"
